Description: Android phone as a Linux virtual webcam
 Okami Cam turns an Android phone into a native Linux virtual webcam over Wi-Fi. The phone streams H264 over the local network and the desktop app feeds it into a v4l2loopback device, so Discord, Teams, Meet, Zoom, OBS and any other V4L2 application see it as an ordinary camera.

